// --- Yield (native runtime; rolling) ---
//
// This file defines a minimal `oren_yield()` surface that matches the AVM intent:
// “yield to other runnable work”.
//
// Native runtime reality today:
// - macOS/Linux: language `spawn` is fork+pipe (process-based), so there is no shared scheduler.
// - Windows: language `spawn` is CreateThread (shared memory), so OS-thread yield is meaningful.
//
// This function is a **best-effort OS yield hint**:
// - Linux: calls sched_yield(2) via syscall-first `sys_sched_yield()`.
// - Windows: calls Sleep(0) via `sys_sched_yield()` shim.
// - macOS: currently a no-op (returns 0); a future native greenlet scheduler will provide a
//   stronger yield contract.
//
// Contract:
// - returns 0 on success; may return -errno on failed syscall paths.
@oren.keep
fn oren_yield() {
    // If we are running inside a native green task, yield to the scheduler (in-process).
    // Otherwise, fall back to the OS yield hint.
    if oren_green_current_g_or0() != 0 {
        return oren_green_yield()
    }
    return sys_sched_yield()
}

@oren.keep
fn oren_yield_stmt() {
    oren_yield()
    return nil
}
